  "title": "India's E100 Flex-Fuel Policy Update and Karnataka's Ethanol Claims",
  "summary": "The Indian government updates its fuel policy to allow 100% ethanol fuel, while the Karnataka government challenges the ethanol content in fuel, citing test results that exceed the prescribed limits. The Supreme Court of India also addresses the use of 'energy drink' labels.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "India's E100 Flex-Fuel Vehicle Policy Update: The Indian government has amended motor vehicle rules to allow vehicles that can run on 100% ethanol fuel, with new guidelines for fuel specifications and classification thresholds.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Karnataka Government's Ethanol Claims: The Karnataka government claims ethanol content in fuel exceeds the allowed limit, citing test results from 11 out of 14 samples in 7 districts, which show higher ethanol levels than prescribed.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "India's Export Duty Cuts: The Indian government reduces the export duty on diesel and aviation fuel to ₹20 per litre, addressing inflationary pressures.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
