  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Citing Karnataka study, Rahul Gandhi says ethanol content in petrol ‘exceeding limit’",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/e20-turned-into-420-petrol-chori-from-publics-cars-rahul-slams-government/article71677541.ece",
      "description": "Union government rejects allegation, questions sampling method used by Karnataka government’s Department of Food, Civil Supplies, Consumer Affairs and Legal Metrology",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-11-07T15:41:46"
    },
    {
      "title": "Centre counters Karnataka's E20 claims, says samples meet quality standards",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/centre-counters-karnataka-s-e20-claims-says-samples-meet-quality-standards-126110700854_1.html",
      "description": "The government on Saturday defended the 20 per cent ethanol-blended petrol programme, saying tests of 893 samples collected across 27 states and Union Territories, including 56 in Karnataka, found them compliant with prescribed quality standards, as state-run oil companies challenged the Karnataka government's claims of excessive ethanol content in fuel sold at some retail outlets.\nThe Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas, in a statement, said Indian Oil Corporation (IOC), Bharat Petroleum Corporation (BPCL) and Hindustan Petroleum Corporation (HPCL) had found ethanol content in all 893 samples within the prescribed 19-21 per cent range under the Bureau of Indian Standards' IS 17021 specification.\nThe 56 samples tested in Karnataka, covering different locations and all three oil marketing companies (OMCs), recorded ethanol content of 19-20 per cent, averaging 19.30 per cent, the ministry said.\nThe findings directly contradict a recent press release by Karnataka's Department of Food",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-07T14:25:33"
    },
    {
      "title": "Rahul questions E20 petrol ethanol levels, cites Karnataka test results",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/rahul-questions-e20-petrol-ethanol-levels-cites-karnataka-test-results-126110700329_1.html",
      "description": "Congress leader Rahul Gandhi on Saturday attacked the Modi government over the rollout of E20 petrol, citing test results of samples collected by the Karnataka government, and asked the Centre to come clean on the actual ethanol content in fuel being sold across the country.\nIn a post in Hindi on X, Gandhi said, \"E20 turned into 420  stealing petrol from the public's cars!\" The reference was to Section 420 of the erstwhile Indian Penal Code, which dealt with cheating.\nGandhi said the government claims that petrol contains 20 per cent ethanol but tests conducted on samples collected from seven districts in Karnataka had revealed higher levels.\n\"The Karnataka government collected petrol samples from 7 districts and had them tested at an accredited lab. Look at the results  11 out of 14 samples contained more than 20 per cent ethanol; 31.2 per cent at IOCL, 30.5 per cent at HPCL; IOCL, HPCL, BPCL, Nayara, Shell  whether government-owned or private  all exceeded the limit,\" he claimed.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-07T08:32:30"
    }
  ]
